# suspend_resume_errors: rvg_device_will_resume's answers for crafted blobs: data shorter than the header, a magic that is not ours (a PGSD blob's included) and malformed sections (one running past the end, an unknown tag, a section repeated or missing, a payload of the wrong length, more than 45 device-info pairs, or a device-info key a resume does not read: 0, 43, 45) are InvalidContent (2); a version other than 1 is InvalidSuspendStateVersion (1). The sections may come in either order, and the device-info max key is carried as it is, negative included. A binary version >= 0xf6, or one the version negotiation rejects (1, 236), is InvalidGuestVersion (3); a port count other than the device's is InvalidDisplayPortCount (5); connection types that differ at version >= 238 are InternalFault (0). A blob setting every register is accepted. The device is never resumed.
